i.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-29T12:55:20Z","updated_at":"2025-03-29T12:55:20Z","body":"> Something like this?\r\n\r\nyes but the right edge of the scrollbar should stay in place when the scrollbar enlarges imo to make sure mouse cursor is still over the scrollbar when that happens, because you normally wouldn't expect a ui element to be clickable/draggable when it's not under the cursor. I also think it could be a bit thicker by default, it appears to be only 1px in the video. blender video that I posted is probably a good reference for both of those things\r\n\r\n> The scrollbar still reserves space, but only 20%\r\n\r\nit's fine, can be further improved in the future by evening out all of the gaps around the scrollable area (by making left/top/right gaps same size) to make the scrollbar space on the right \"invisible\" when the scrollbar is hidden","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2763352928/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2763362344","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104605#issuecomment-2763362344","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104605","id":2763362344,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ktZAo","user":{"login":"RY-Storm","id":143893793,"node_id":"U_kgDOCJOlIQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143893793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RY-Storm","html_url":"https://github.com/RY-Storm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RY-Storm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RY-Storm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RY-Storm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RY-Storm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RY-Storm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RY-Storm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RY-Storm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RY-Storm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RY-Storm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-29T13:23:06Z","updated_at":"2025-03-29T13:24:23Z","body":">  right edge of the scrollbar should stay in place when the scrollbar enlarges imo\r\n\r\nAgreed, the Blender example of it growing while its right edge stays put inside the reserved area is good. \r\nIn the video above the scrollbar looks like it 'runs away' from the mouse, as it moves left entirely.\r\n\r\nOne other thing that would be good to check is: On the triple dot menus and dropdowns in the above video: Does moving the mouse over them trigger the scrollbar too enlarge, and cover the element? That would be frustrating.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2763362344/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"